--- !u!114 &7063624849794940585
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6821381671391748898}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "\tSecretary of the Navy R. Funderburg\u2019s body was recovered from an
    inlet of Puget Sound early this morning after being spotted by local ferry passengers.
    His personal vehicle was found unlocked and with significant signs of struggle,
    leading to suspicions of murder. No official details have been released regarding
    the cause of his death.\r\n\tRichard Funderburg took on the role only two years
    ago, with hefty promises to oversee the renovation of homeland naval architecture
    to accommodate the expansion of naval military operations. His most recent project
    involved the Puget Sound Naval Shipyard, which is expected to see employment
    growth of up to 200% by the end of this year. According to local sources, construction
    had frequently been delayed or halted, and Funderburg announced in October that
    he would be personally visiting the site with the intention to \u201Cenforce
    compliance for the good of the safety of the American people.\u201D \r\n\tPassengers
    on an early-morning ferry from Bremerton to Seattle alerted police to what appeared
    to be a body floating in the Sinclair Inlet, and police quickly recovered and
    identified the corpse. Funderburg\u2019s hotel room was searched, yielding nothing
    out of the ordinary, but his car was discovered near PSNS, with both front doors
    unlocked and with severe bloodstaining in the driver\u2019s seat and carpet.
    It is unclear whether Funderburg was alive when he entered the inlet, and no
    further details have been made available as to the cause of death or potential
    agitators. \r\nWithout Funderburg\u2019s initiative, inside sources it is unlikely
    that his projects at PSNS will move forward.\r\n\r\n\tThis story is still developing. "
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0445602e006599347a14a022e954282d, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: -3527436854880083569, guid: 0445602e006599347a14a022e954282d, type: 2}
